span>Lala Lajpat Rai wrote 'Unhappy India' (1928) as a strong rebuttal to Katherine Mayo's controversial and one-sided book 'Mother India', which had portrayed Indian society in a highly critical and biased light.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"31143","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"834","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is a UNESCO World Heritage Site?</span></p>","option_1":"Kamakhya Temple","option_2":"Meenakshi Temple","option_3":"Kashi Vishwanath Temple","option_4":"Gangaikonda Cholapuram Temple","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Gangaikonda Cholapuram Temple.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Gangaikonda Cholapuram Temple, built by the Chola king Rajendra I, is part of the 'Great Living Chola Temples' group, which has been designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The other temples listed, though significant, do not hold this designation.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"31144","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"834","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus is located in which of the following city?</span></p>","option_1":"Mumbai","option_2":"Kolkata","option_3":"Delhi","option_4":"Ahmadabad","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Mumbai.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (formerly Victoria Terminus), a UNESCO World Heritage Site and a major railway station, is located in Mumbai, Maharashtra.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"31145","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"834","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is a correct use of electromagnets?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>I. In separating magnetic material from junk</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>II. In sharpening pencils</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Only I.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Electromagnets are widely used in scrapyards to separate magnetic materials (like iron and steel) from junk/waste, since their magnetic field can be switched on and off using electric current. Sharpening pencils has no connection to electromagnetism, so only statement I is correct.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""}]